  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint, because the target has at least two fully separate attack paths. Path A: wifiGuest/vpnGateway -> kerberoast:credentialAccess (OR) -> backupHost:lateralMovement (OR) -> codeRepo:collection (OR) -> crownData:exfiltrate. Path B: vpnGateway/phishing -> mailClient:execution -> tokenCache:credentialAccess; vpnGateway -> ciRunner:execution -> memoryDump:credentialAccess (supplychain also feeds memoryDump). Then rdpLogin:authenticate (AND of tokenCache and memoryDump) -> printServer:lateralMovement (OR) -> shareMount:collection (OR) -> crownData:exfiltrate. The two paths share no intermediate steps, so blocking any one step leaves the other path intact. Other routes also exist, such as dbLogin -> jumpHost -> dbReplica."
